cs, Sheets, or Slides. You can read it, edit it, and comment on it. Your changes are saved back to the original Office file."}]]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Office editing: keep the Office format"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","ul","0",{"className":"list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:text-primary-500","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"An Office file shows its file type in a small chip next to the name at the top left, such as .DOCX, .XLSX, or .PPTX."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Edits save automatically, in the Office format. Someone who downloads the file later gets a normal Word, Excel, or PowerPoint file."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Drive's Office editing works with Word (.doc, .docx, .dot), Excel (.xls, .xlsx, .xlsm, .xlt), and PowerPoint (.ppt, .pptx, .pps, .pot) files."}]]}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Some features work only in Google files, such as protected ranges in Sheets, add-ons, Apps Script, and translating a document. To use them, convert the file: open it, then choose File › Save as Google Docs (or Save as Google Sheets, Save as Google Slides)."}],["$","div","2",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-blue-50 border-blue-400","children":[false,"Converting makes a copy. The original Office file stays in Drive, unchanged, and the new Google file opens in a new tab. Rename or delete the one you do not need so coworkers do not edit the wrong copy."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","2",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Download as Office or PDF"}],"$L1f"]}],"$L20"]}]}]]}]
